cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the SE–BCT sequencing framework in your research, please cite the associated paper below. The archived interactive resource is also identified by its Zenodo DOI."

type: software
title: "Interactive SE–BCT Sequencing Framework"
version: 1.0.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22047154"

authors:
  - family-names: "Mazéas"
    given-names: "Alexandre"
  - family-names: "Ntoumanis"
    given-names: "Nikos"

abstract: >-
  An interactive web-based resource for exploring the proposed sequencing
  of self-enactable behavior change techniques (SE-BCTs). Users can navigate
  clusters and groups, examine when groups are proposed to be most relevant
  across the behavior-change process, and view individual SE-BCTs together
  with their mode of enactment and, where applicable, prerequisite techniques.

license: MIT

keywords:
  - behavior change
  - behavior change techniques
  - self-enactable behavior change techniques
  - SE-BCT
  - intervention development
  - sequencing

